artists/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appsforartists/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appsforartists/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appsforartists/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-12-21T18:46:54Z","updated_at":"2014-12-21T18:46:54Z","body":"Sorry - I should not reply to GitHub issues at 6 AM.\n\nI just looked at the options being passed into DefinePlugin, and they look like this:\n\n``` json\n{ \n  \"__ambidexSettings\":                      \"...\",\n  \"__ambidexRoutesPath\":                    \"\\\"/Users/bresimpson/Projects/tardis/routes.jsx\\\"\",\n  \"__ambidexRefluxDefinitionsPath\":         undefined,\n  \"__ambidexCallActionsForRouterStatePath\": undefined \n}\n```\n\nwhich is generated by this:\n\n``` javascript\n{\n  \"__ambidexSettings\":                        settings,\n  \"__ambidexRoutesPath\":                      self._get(\"routesPath\"),\n  \"__ambidexRefluxDefinitionsPath\":           self._get(\"refluxDefinitionsPath\"),\n  \"__ambidexCallActionsForRouterStatePath\":   self._get(\"callActionsForRouterStatePath\"),\n}\n```\n\nAfter [re-reading the DefinePlugin docs](http://webpack.github.io/docs/list-of-plugins.html#defineplugin), I can see that it's trying to `JSON.stringify(undefined)`.  I'm guessing that when it doesn't get a string back, from that function, it drop the whole key,value pair.\n\nThat's all well-and-good, but it shouldn't happen silently.  If DefinePlugin gets something it doesn't know how to parse, it should throw a warning:\n\n```\n\"Cannot stringify `\"__ambidexRefluxDefinitionsPath\":  undefined`; so it's been ignored.\"\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/67779980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":